1. Functional Requirements

📥 File Processing Lifecycle

* System shall ingest files from:
    * SFTP / object storage
* Each file shall be uniquely identified (file_id)
* Each file shall go through states:
    * PENDING → PROCESSING → SUCCESS / FAILED

⸻

⚙️ Job Orchestration

* System shall create processing jobs dynamically per file
* Each job shall:
    * Process exactly one file (recommended)
    * Be stateless and idempotent
* System shall support parallel execution of jobs

⸻

🔢 Concurrency Control

* System shall enforce maximum parallel job limit (MAX_PARALLEL)
* System shall:
    * Read pending records from DB
    * Spawn jobs only if capacity is available
* System shall prevent duplicate processing using DB locking

⸻

🔁 Retry Management

* System shall support:
    * Automatic retry (configurable max attempts)
    * Manual retry via API/UI
* Failed jobs shall be eligible for retry
* Retry shall create a new job instance

⸻

📊 Monitoring & Tracking

* System shall track:
    * Job status
    * Start/end time
    * Retry count
    * Processing node/pod
* System shall provide APIs/UI to:
    * View job status
    * Filter/search jobs
    * View logs

⸻

📜 Logging

* System shall provide:
    * Access to job logs (via Kubernetes)
    * Correlation using correlation_id

⸻

🌍 Multi-Data Center Support

* System shall support:
    * Active–Active OR Active–Passive modes
* System shall avoid duplicate processing across DCs
* System shall maintain a global processing state

⸻

🔐 Security

* System shall use:
    * Role-based access control (RBAC)
    * Secure secrets for SFTP, DB
* No direct cluster-admin usage

⸻

🧱 2. Technical Requirements

⸻

☸️ Platform

* Container orchestration:
    * Kubernetes (OpenShift compatible)
* Jobs shall be executed using:
    * Kubernetes Jobs (batch/v1)

⸻

🧠 Coordinator Service

Technology

* ASP.NET Core (.NET Worker/API)

Responsibilities

* Read DB for pending jobs
* Enforce MAX_PARALLEL limit
* Create Kubernetes Jobs via API (not CLI)
* Track job lifecycle
* Provide REST APIs

Must support:

* Non-blocking async job submission
* Background reconciliation loop

⸻

🗄 Database Layer

Use:

* PostgreSQL

Schema (simplified)

file_jobs (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
  file_path TEXT,
  status TEXT,
  retry_count INT,
  locked_by TEXT,
  locked_at TIMESTAMP,
  created_at TIMESTAMP,
  updated_at TIMESTAMP
)

Distributed Locking

* Use DB-based locking:
    * FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
* Ensure:
    * No duplicate job pickup
    * Safe multi-instance coordinator

⸻

⚙️ Job Execution

Each Kubernetes Job shall:

* Run a containerized worker
* Accept input via ENV variables
* Exit with:
    * 0 → success
    * non-zero → failure

⸻

🔄 Job Lifecycle Management

Coordinator shall:

* Create jobs asynchronously
* Track via:
    * Kubernetes Watch API (preferred)
    * or polling

⸻

🔁 Retry Mechanism

* DB-driven retry:
    * Increment retry count
    * Reset status to PENDING
* Optional:
    * Dead-letter handling

⸻

📡 Optional Messaging Layer (Recommended for scale)

Use:

* RabbitMQ
    or
* Apache Kafka

Purpose:

* Decouple ingestion from processing
* Enable multi-DC distribution
* Improve throughput

⸻

📦 Storage Layer

* Object storage / SFTP:
    * MinIO (self-hosted)
    * or cloud equivalent

⸻

📊 Observability

Use:

* Prometheus
* Grafana

Track:

* active jobs
* queue depth / pending records
* failures / retries
* processing latency

⸻

📜 Logging

* Use centralized logging:
    * ELK Stack
* Logs sourced from Kubernetes pods

⸻

🔐 Security & Access

* Use ServiceAccount for coordinator
* RBAC permissions:
    * create/list/watch jobs
    * read pod logs

⸻

🌍 Multi-DC Architecture

Option 1 (Recommended)

* Active–Active with shared DB + MQ

Option 2

* Active–Passive with leader election

⸻

⚡ Performance & Scaling

* Horizontal scaling:
    * multiple coordinator instances
    * multiple worker pods
* Auto-scaling:
    * based on queue depth or CPU

⸻

🔁 3. End-to-End Flow

1. File arrives (SFTP / storage)
2. DB record created (PENDING)
3. Coordinator polls DB
4. Claims records (SKIP LOCKED)
5. Creates Kubernetes Jobs
6. Worker processes file
7. Worker updates DB (SUCCESS/FAILED)
8. Coordinator tracks status
9. Retry triggered if needed

4. Non-Functional Requirements

Reliability

* Idempotent processing
* Automatic retries
* Recovery for stuck jobs

Scalability

* Handle increasing file volume
* Support horizontal scaling

Availability

* Multi-DC capable
* No single point of failure

Maintainability

* Modular services
* Clear separation:
    * coordinator vs worker

⸻

💡 5. Key Design Decisions

* ❌ No file watchers
* ❌ No manual AutoSys jobs
* ❌ No blocking threads
* ❌ No kubectl/oc inside app
* ✅ DB-driven orchestration
* ✅ Kubernetes-native Jobs
* ✅ Async processing
* ✅ Idempotency-first design

⸻

🧠 Final Architecture Summary

* Coordinator → decides what & when
* Database → controls state & concurrency
* Kubernetes → executes work in parallel
* (Optional MQ) → distributes load across systems

